    "episode_id": "VR-478203",
    "evidence": "The timesheet does not support 42 hours on either principled reading of 'worked'.\n\nPer-day hours worked (clock-out minus clock-in minus the recorded unpaid break):\n  Mon 19 Oct: 08:00-16:30 = 8h 30m, less 30m = 8h 00m\n  Tue 20 Oct: 08:00-17:00 = 9h 00m, less 45m = 8h 15m\n  Wed 21 Oct: 07:30-16:00 = 8h 30m, less 30m = 8h 00m\n  Thu 22 Oct: 08:00-16:15 = 8h 15m, less 30m = 7h 45m\n  Fri 23 Oct: 08:00-17:00 = 9h 00m, less 30m = 8h 30m\n  Sat 24 / Sun 25 Oct: no clock times, no hours.\n  Total hours worked = 2,430 minutes = 40.5 hours.\n\nGross time on site, before any break deduction, is 2,595 minutes = 43.25 hours.\n\nThe claimed 42 hours (2,520 minutes) matches neither figure. The record states breaks are unpaid and deducted from time on site, so 40.5 hours is the measure of hours worked - 1.5 hours short of the claim. The only way to reach exactly 42 hours is to deduct 75 of the 165 recorded break minutes, i.e. to disregard 90 minutes of recorded unpaid breaks; no line of the sheet supports that. Even the most generous reading (no breaks deducted at all) gives 43.25, not 42.\n\nI record the honest caveat that 'worked' could be read as gross attendance (43.25 hours), but that reading also fails to produce 42, so the claim is unsupported either way.",
